          "scenario": "Inspection exposes semantic identity rather than AppKit object identity; automation actions route through the normal event/authorization path.",
          "reason": "client-macos/Accessibility is a 4-line placeholder; no inspection or automation API exists on this base.",
          "future_task": "Task 35 (local semantic inspection and automation API)",
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            "Inspection results are keyed by semantic NodeId, never by NSView identity.",
            "Each inspected node exposes role, label, value, hierarchy position, and available actions.",
            "Automation actions are dispatched through EventOutbox, not by invoking AppKit targets directly.",
            "Actions on a disabled node are refused with the same authorization path as user input.",
            "No AppKit type appears in the public inspection API surface."
          ],
